{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/upgrade.py and upgrade the catalog from v1 to v2 while preserving existing IDs and descriptions, adding a non-null nonnegative price_cents field initialized to zero.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script was installed and the live upgrade completed. The resulting database has schema version 2, retains products (1, Paper) and (2, Tape), initializes both prices to 0, defaults new prices to 0, rejects negative and NULL values, and passes integrity checks. The same state remained healthy after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cca9c45bc7f43e9","cmd-636e27f8add34a17","cmd-de6189d1ba034637"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the upgrade transactional so schema_version advances only after the whole upgrade succeeds and a failed attempt leaves the v1 database usable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The script encloses schema alteration and version update in one explicit transaction with rollback on exceptions. A forced failure during the version update rolled back the preceding ALTER: version stayed 1, the original two-column schema and rows remained, integrity was OK, and a v1 write succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cca9c45bc7f43e9","cmd-74959c3621bd473a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make the migration safe to repeat.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A second execution completed successfully with exactly three columns, unchanged rows, version 2, and an unchanged database checksum. A further post-restart execution was also successful and checksum-neutral.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e0ec3ef887f42a7","cmd-de6189d1ba034637"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The executor used the platform's installed Python 3 and SQLite library without package or platform replacement. RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were directly observed both before work and after restart, matching the lifecycle snapshots; package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-af1f0e4802ef4f96","cmd-de6189d1ba034637","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The script replacement and live database upgrade directly implemented the task; isolated temporary database, trigger, compiled bytecode, checksum, and backup files supported bounded failure/repeatability testing and were removed; rolled-back data probes left no rows; and the reboot/transient unit served the mandatory provider restart protocol. Final evidence shows only the intended three project files, no failed services, healthy package state, and unchanged listener exposure. Restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged scheduled restart, observed interruption, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered services, data, constraints, integrity, and repeatability; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree. Reboot-created systemd private temporary directories and changed service PIDs are expected recovered-runtime state, not residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7cca9c45bc7f43e9","cmd-74959c3621bd473a","cmd-636e27f8add34a17","cmd-7e0ec3ef887f42a7","cmd-cde4e15d87bf43bb","cmd-cd57f9c944204180","cmd-b0568bc429364bad","cmd-c654ef1071cd4368","cmd-de6189d1ba034637","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The catalog was upgraded transactionally to v2 with preserved data and enforced price semantics; forced failure demonstrated complete rollback to usable v1; repeated runs were checksum-neutral; and the installed OS and kernel were preserved. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also fully and coherently demonstrated.","limitations":[]}
